new workflow:
- linter. checks formatting. if ok then runs 2 next tasks in parallel
- check. does `cargo check` of trappist and stout to make sure that the code compiles
- test. runs `cargo test --features runtime-benchmarks` to execute all tests including benchmarks

github runners don't have limited space and memory. the following things were done to make tests runable:
- free disk space by removing unused components from Ubuntu image;
- keep check and test versions separately in cache;
- limit number of threads used by cargo. if a runner fails with error `Process completed with exit code 143.` number of threads might be reduced to 1;

