## Purpose
https://issues.folio.org/browse/UIU-2805

If users are able to have multiple affiliations there must be a way to adjust the permissions associated with that affiliation.

## Approach
- Apply changes related to the refactoring of consortium data fetch (#2462);
- Inject `<AffiliationsSelect>` component to `<PermissionsAccordion>` if the current user is in the scope of a consortium affiliation and is assigned to more than one affiliation;
- Implement `<TenantsPermissionsAccordion>` component to render a permissions list for the selected affiliation (tenant);
- Display affiliations in the selection, that are only assigned to a current user (who edits a user; `assignedToCurrentUser` flag in the `useUserAffiliations` hook);
- Update `<PermissionsModal>` to fetch permissions from the defined tenant;
- Handle user's permissions update in each tenant (`UserEdit.js::updatePermissions`);
- Update unit tests.
